      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:38:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right this can and should be included here.\nAdded --max-spdm-message-size to the daemon in this change. Platform service\nconfiguration can pass the limit at startup, for example\nspdmd --max-spdm-message-size 2047. The daemon validates the value before\ndiscovery and passes it to each discovered MCTP responder, including\ninitialization retries and runtime additions. The default remains 4608 bytes.\nAdded option-validation and responder-configuration tests and usage documentation.",
      "parentUuid": "f5258ed1_3193e121",
      "revId": "aab28235b6de66aab8019c0eef0881b3a8ec61aa",
